NAME
     dirty - dirty memory at a set rate

SYNOPSIS
     dirty MB RATE SECONDS

DESCRIPTION
     dirty takes MB megabytes of memory, writes all of it, then rewrites
     RATE megabytes of it a second for SECONDS, cycling through the region
     so that every page is dirtied again and again. Each write is a pattern
     keyed by the address and the round, and at the end the last round is
     verified: a page copied stale by a migration shows as a mismatch. It
     is the tunable dirtier behind the migration curves.

SEE ALSO
     memck(1), cksum(1)
